---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us & Our Review Methodology"
  description="Learn how the Productivity Software Reviews editorial team researches, evaluates, and compares SaaS tools for small business owners and creators."
>
  <div class="prose-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="badge">About the Publication</span>
      <h1>Software Reviews Written for Small Teams and Independent Creators</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        Produced by the <strong>Productivity Software Reviews editorial team</strong> to help small business owners, agencies, and creators choose reliable software without drowning in bloated feature matrices.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2>Why We Started Productivity Software Reviews</h2>
      <p>
        If you run a 5-person agency, a solo consulting practice, or a growing creator business, choosing software can quickly become overwhelming. Many software directories either repeat vendor marketing slogans verbatim or evaluate tools from the perspective of a 500-person corporate IT department.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Productivity Software Reviews</strong> was built by our editorial team to bridge that gap. We focus specifically on how modern SaaS tools fit lean teams where every subscription dollar and every hour of setup time matters.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Review Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Our reviews are based on hands-on time with free plans and trials, official documentation and pricing, and aggregated user feedback.</strong> Rather than claiming multi-month enterprise deployments, we focus on transparent, practical research across three core pillars:
      </p>

      <div class="method-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1. Official Documentation &amp; Pricing Analysis</h3>
          <p>
            We carefully audit official vendor documentation, feature specifications, and pricing pages to uncover seat minimums, tier restrictions, and true annual vs. monthly costs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2. Free Plan &amp; Free Trial Exploration</h3>
          <p>
            We use available free tiers and trial accounts to check interface clarity, initial setup friction, template quality, and core everyday features firsthand.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3. Aggregated User &amp; Community Feedback</h3>
          <p>
            We synthesize public user reviews and long-term community discussions to identify recurring pain points, learning curves, performance issues, and support quality.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>4. Clear Editorial Scores &amp; "Best For" Verdicts</h3>
          <p>
            No single tool is right for everyone. Our editorial team assigns an Editorial Score (out of 5.0) and states plainly who should consider a tool—and who should skip it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Editorial Independence</h2>
      <p>
        Our editorial team operates independently from our affiliate partnerships. Software vendors cannot pay to be included in our comparisons, cannot pay to raise their Editorial Score, and do not preview or edit our articles before publication. For full details on how this site is funded, please read our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header h1 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .method-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 2.25rem;
  }

  .method-grid h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .method-grid p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .method-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
